<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.5.1: Writing and Evaluating New Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00441</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.5.1: Writing and Evaluating New Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>69f7a23d-d07a-4c1c-a322-d20216bd388d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Look at the following equation: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>

          <para id="para-00002">Perform each of the following operations and answer these questions: What does each
            resulting equation look like? Is it still a true equation?</para>

      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Add 12 to each side of the equation.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer:</para>

          <para id="para-00005"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>63</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>63</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (or equivalent). Yes, it is still a true
            equation.</para>

        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Question
      2-->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
         <para id="para-00006">Add <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> to the left side of the equation and 12 to the right side.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
         <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer:</para>

          <para id="para-00008"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>63</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>63</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (or equivalent). Yes, it is still a
            true equation.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Question
      3-->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">Add the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> to the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
        <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>

          <para id="para-00011"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>58</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>58</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (or equivalent). Yes, it is still a true
            equation.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Question
      4-->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00012">Write a new equation that, when added to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, gives a sum that is
            also a true equation.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
     <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00014">Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>

          <list id="list-00001">
            <item><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. Added to the original equation gives: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>51</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>61</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>61</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>61</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
            <item><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. Added to the original equation gives: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>51</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
          </list>

        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Question
      5-->
      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00015"> 5. Write a new equation that, when added to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, gives a sum that is a
            false equation.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
   <para id="para-00016">Compare your answer:</para>

          <para id="para-00017">Your answer may vary, but here are some samples</para>

          <list id="list-00002">
            <item><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. Added to the original equation gives: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>,
              or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>56</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>58</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, which is false.</item>
            <item><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. Added to the original equation gives: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>,
              or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>53</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>51</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, which is false.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
